  m_Name: LS Edge Length Tessellation
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_functionInfo: "// Made with Amplify Shader Editor v1.9.9.9\n// Available at the
    Unity Asset Store - http://u3d.as/y3X \n/*ASEBEGIN\nVersion=19909\nNode;AmplifyShaderEditor.CommentaryNode,
    AmplifyShaderEditor, Version=0.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null;65;-1024,-1152;Inherit;False;630.2465;204.3754;Edge
    Length Tessellation Node;2;15;8;;0,0,0,1;0;0\nNode;AmplifyShaderEditor.CommentaryNode,
    AmplifyShaderEditor, Version=0.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null;59;-1024,-1680;Inherit;False;1916.82;456.3367;Edge
    Length Tessellation Node;5;67;66;64;63;60;;0,0,0,1;0;0\nNode;AmplifyShaderEditor.StickyNoteNode,
    AmplifyShaderEditor, Version=0.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null;60;-992,-1632;Inherit;False;348.556;142.1179;Edge
    Length;;0,0,0,1;Desired final tessellated edge length in pixels;0;0\nNode;AmplifyShaderEditor.StickyNoteNode,
    AmplifyShaderEditor, Version=0.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null;63;-336,-1632;Inherit;False;717.4745;195.582;;;0,0,0,1;The
    Edge Length Tessellation Node sets up tessellation according to an object triangles
    edge length on screen. $$This technique allows the subdivision of a mesh's triangles,
    splitting them into smaller triangles at run-time in order to increase the surface
    detail of any given mesh. $$On this node in particular a desired final edge length
    is set via the Edge Length parameter which makes longer edges have a larger tessellation
    factor applied to them;0;0\nNode;AmplifyShaderEditor.StickyNoteNode, AmplifyShaderEditor,
    Version=0.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null;64;-336,-1424;Inherit;False;716.6146;146.0653;NOTE;;0,0,0,1;Using
    this node is equivalent to activate the Tessellation option on the Master Node
    and set its Type to Edge Length. The Shader Model will be automatically set to
    4.6 if its set to a lower value, since its the minimum version required.;0;0\nNode;AmplifyShaderEditor.EdgeLengthTessNode,
    AmplifyShaderEditor, Version=0.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null;15;-688,-1088;Inherit;False;1;0;FLOAT;0;False;1;FLOAT4;0\nNode;AmplifyShaderEditor.EdgeLengthTessNode,
    AmplifyShaderEditor, Version=0.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null;66;-592,-1632;Inherit;False;1;0;FLOAT;0;False;1;FLOAT4;0\nNode;AmplifyShaderEditor.RangedFloatNode,
    AmplifyShaderEditor, Version=0.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null;8;-976,-1088;Half;False;Property;_TessellationStrength;Tessellation
    Strength;0;0;Create;False;1;;0;0;False;0;False;0.0001;0.5;0.0001;250;0;1;FLOAT;0\nNode;AmplifyShaderEditor.StickyNoteNode,
    AmplifyShaderEditor, Version=0.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null;67;416,-1632;Inherit;False;445.2001;213.6;Note;;0,0,0,1;Regenerate
    post-tessellated normal => Just write to \"Vertex Offset\" or \"Vertex Normal\".
    We made it so that it automatically displaces AFTER tessellation.$$Pull post-tessellated
    normal => We're intentionally running the vertex shader code AFTER tessellation
    (in domain stage), so the \"Vertex Normal\" should be post-tessellation.;0;0\nNode;AmplifyShaderEditor.FunctionOutput,
    AmplifyShaderEditor, Version=0.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=null;10;-1024,-1792;Inherit;False;True;-1;Out;0;True;1;0;FLOAT;0;False;1;FLOAT;0\nWireConnection;15;0;8;0\nASEEND*/\n//CHKSM=28C0DB2DEAE27DBCDA03560656CA6243F717DF9C"
